From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] cgame: an attach point for drawing our own readouts

The ship's state at a panel is drawn in the world's HUD, which only cgame draws. This adds the one
seam that lets our module do it: a header whose call is empty unless LWH_MODULE_DIR is set, and a
single call in CG_Draw2D. The logic is in module/cgame/, not here.
---
diff --git a/efgame/src/cgame/cg_draw.cpp b/efgame/src/cgame/cg_draw.cpp
index e149bbc..d9efeed 100755
--- a/efgame/src/cgame/cg_draw.cpp
+++ b/efgame/src/cgame/cg_draw.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include "../game/speakers.h"
 #include "../speedrun/PlayerOverbouncePrediction.hpp"
 #include "../speedrun/strafe_helper/strafe_helper.h"
+#include "lwh_cgame_hooks.h"
 #include <cmath>
 
 
@@ -2494,6 +2495,7 @@ static void CG_Draw2D( void )
 		CG_DrawAmmoWarning();
 		CG_DrawCrosshair();
 		CG_DrawCrosshairNames();
+		LWH_CG_DrawPanelGlance(); // Long Way Home: the ship's state at the panel being looked at
 		CG_DrawTED();
 		CG_DrawWeaponSelect();
 		CG_DrawPickupItem();
diff --git a/efgame/src/cgame/lwh_cgame_hooks.h b/efgame/src/cgame/lwh_cgame_hooks.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f29f056
--- /dev/null
+++ b/efgame/src/cgame/lwh_cgame_hooks.h
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+// lwh_cgame_hooks.h -- where Long Way Home's own client (cgame) drawing attaches to cgame.
+//
+// Like game/lwh_hooks.h and ui/lwh_ui_hooks.h: the logic itself is not in this tree. It is compiled
+// in from LWH_MODULE_DIR (which defines LWH_CREW) as module/cgame/*.cpp. Without it this is an empty
+// inline and cgame draws exactly as upstream does.
+
+#ifndef LWH_CGAME_HOOKS_H
+#define LWH_CGAME_HOOKS_H
+
+#ifdef LWH_CREW
+void LWH_CG_DrawPanelGlance( void );
+#else
+inline void LWH_CG_DrawPanelGlance( void ) {}
+#endif
+
+#endif
